244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (Grouping raw ridership data, well over a million rows, directly inside Power BI / Power Query was the wrong call.  It's what drove the 12+ hour calculation times and for the station-level grouping a 10-hour compute plus a further 5 hours just to save the result.)
/E (Grouping raw ridership data, well over a million rows, directly inside Power BI / Power Query was the wrong call.  It's what drove the 12+ hour calculation times and for the station-level grouping a 10-hour compute plus a further 5 hours just to save the result.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (With more time, that heavy grouping and transformation would move to a proper data platform. Something like Snowflake or Databricks to built for large-scale processing, leaving Power BI to do what it does best: reporting and visualization on top of clean, pre-aggregated data.)
/E (With more time, that heavy grouping and transformation would move to a proper data platform. Something like Snowflake or Databricks to built for large-scale processing, leaving Power BI to do what it does best: reporting and visualization on top of clean, pre-aggregated data.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
